			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Update Grove.proto field names to PascalCase\n\nConvert all protobuf message field names from snake_case to PascalCase to align with the project's naming conventions as specified in CLAUDE.md.\n\nKey changes:\n- Package name: `grove.v1` → `Grove`\n- All message fields: `extension_id` → `ExtensionId`, `display_name` → `DisplayName`, `activation_events` → `ActivationEvents`, etc.\n- Added explicit `syntax = \"proto3\";` declaration\n\nAlso apply minor formatting consistency: comment style fixes in vscode.rs and CommonAdapter.rs, import consolidation in build.rs, and whitespace normalization in extension_loading_test.rs.\n\nThis is a breaking change to the gRPC protocol - consumers of the GroveService will need to update their field references.",
			"SHA": "8eeb25ebbc3153c797558a9cd3b77ef57e70c1c8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T05:11:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Grove): Fix import path to use PascalCase module name\n\nUpdate the import statement in Source/main.rs to use `Grove` (PascalCase) instead of `grove` (lowercase), aligning with the project's naming conventions as specified in CLAUDE.md.\n\nThis ensures consistency with the project's PascalCase naming standard for modules and crates.",
			"SHA": "80c11d254d18fa3a42f94b33840df8b33082f818"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:53:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				71,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Grove): Fix string ownership in LanguageNamespace provider registration\n\nThe `provider_type` parameter was being used as a borrowed `&str` reference in multiple places within the `register()` method, causing potential lifetime issues when passed to `store.insert()` and used in `format!()` calls.\n\nNow the method converts `provider_type` to an owned `String` (`ProviderTypeOwned`) first, then passes a reference to that owned string to `store.insert()`. This ensures consistent ownership semantics and eliminates the reference-to-temporary issue.\n\nAlso: simplify import paths in the module header and apply minor formatting consistency across method signatures.",
			"SHA": "fbe35236c67dc54460c427bf80634673e4a3dd6d"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781544260551
}